      "notes": "**Scope note:** The Q2 FY27 earnings report and the related analyst moves were on 2026-09-01 and 2026-09-02. That is before your window, so they appear only as context.\n\n## 1. Guidance\n- No guidance change, pre-announcement or withdrawal found for 2026-09-15 to 2026-10-15.\n- Context: \nQ2 FY27 revenue was $286.3M, up 21% year over year\n — 2026-09-01 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001653482/000162828026059820/gitlab-ex99120260731fy27.htm\n- Context: \nQ3 revenue guidance is $281–283M and FY27 revenue guidance is $1.129–1.133B\n — 2026-09-01 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/GTLB/8-k-gitlab-inc-reports-material-event-2d67542ef44a.html\n- Context: \nFY27 non-GAAP operating income guidance is $148–152M and EPS guidance is $0.85–0.87\n — 2026-09-01 — https://www.alphaspread.com/security/nasdaq/gtlb/investor-relations (aggregator; the primary 8-K gives the same operating income range via the Stocktitan summary above)\n- The next earnings date is \nDec 7, 2026 (listed as confirmed)\n. — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/gtlb/earnings\n\n## 2. Analyst actions\n- I found no upgrades, downgrades, initiations or price-target changes dated inside the window. The Sept 2 actions below are outside it.\n- William Blair upgraded the stock from Underperform to Market Perform — 2026-09-02 — https://www.streetinsider.com/Analyst+Comments/William+Blair+Upgrades+GitLab+Inc+(GTLB)+to+Market+Perform/27014659.html\n- Price-target changes on 2026-09-02, from a secondary aggregator. The page was updated in October, so some later actions may be missing.\n  - \nB of A Securities (Neutral) $45 to $54; Baird (Outperform) $47 to $59; Barclays (Underweight) $25 to $47; BTIG (Buy) $52 to $60; Canaccord (Buy) $40 to $70; Cantor Fitzgerald (Neutral) $50\n — https://tickernerd.com/stock/gtlb-forecast/\n  - \nBernstein (Buy) $60; DA Davidson (Hold) $55; UBS (Hold) $50; TD Cowen (Hold) $55\n — https://www.investing.com/equities/gitlab-consensus-estimates\n- The consensus target is \n$55.71, with a high of $70 and a low of $45\n — date unknown — https://www.investing.com/equities/gitlab-consensus-estimates\n\n## 3. Litigation and regulation\n- Nothing new found in the window.\n- Background: the securities class action (Dolly v. GitLab) was \ndismissed with prejudice, with final judgment entered for GitLab on January 26, 2026\n. — 2026-01-26 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1653482/000165348226000087/a2026gitlabars.pdf\n- The same filing says \nthree putative shareholder derivative cases were filed with similar allegations\n. I did not find their current status. — date unknown — same URL.\n\n## 4. Customer concentration\n- No big customer wins or losses found in the window.\n- Concentration is low. \nNo single customer was more than 10% of revenue in the three months ended April 30, 2026\n. — 2026-04-30 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001653482/000162828026039793/gtlb-20260430.htm\n- I did not retrieve the Q2 10-Q customer-concentration text.\n- Large customers matter to ARR. \n1,519 customers pay over $100,000 a year, and they account for more than 75% of ARR\n. — 2026-06-02 (Q1 call) — https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/03/gitlab-gtlb-q1-2027-earnings-transcript/\n- GitLab is promoting a webinar with NatWest on single-tenant SaaS. — 2026-10-27 — https://about.gitlab.com/events/\n\n## 5. Insider activity\nMost Sept 16 entries are tax-withholding code \"F\" dispositions on RSU vesting, not discretionary sales. Only the CTO and Sijbrandij sales were under 10b5-1 plans.\n- CFO Jessica Ross: \n32,628 shares withheld for taxes at $48.77, leaving 498,157\n — 2026-09-16 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001653482/000165348226000166/wk-form4_1789768598.xml\n  - One aggregator described this as an insider sale of about $1.6M (https://tickernerd.com/stock/gtlb-forecast/). The Form 4 shows it was tax withholding.\n- CRO Ian Steward: \n12,613 shares withheld at $48.77\n — 2026-09-16 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001653482/000165348226000165/wk-form4_1789768128.xml\n- CTO Sivaprasad Padisetty: \n30,888 shares withheld at $48.77\n — 2026-09-16 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001653482/000165348226000167/wk-form4_1789768937.xml\n- Simon Mundy also filed a Form 4 for the same date (signed 2026-09-18). The snippet shows no share count. — 2026-09-16 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001653482/000165348226000164/wk-form4_1789767773.xml\n- Padisetty open-market sales under a 10b5-1 plan adopted June 29, 2026 — 2026-09-28:\n  - \n12,900 shares at $44.83; 33,095 at $46.05; 5,920 at $46.32\n, about 51,915 shares in total, leaving 377,211.\n  - https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001653482/000165348226000171/wk-form4_1790636307.xml\n- Sytse Sijbrandij (trust) sold shares under a 10b5-1 plan adopted June 25, 2026, at weighted-average ranges of roughly $44–49. — date unknown, but the price ranges fall within late September — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001653482/000165348226000170/wk-form4_1790635890.xml\n  - The snippet did not show share counts or dates.\n- I found no insider purchases.\n\n## 6. Product and competitive news\n- GitLab 19.4 was released with \nnew agentic automation at a lower cost\n. — 2026-09-17 — https://about.gitlab.com/press/\n- At Transcend on 2026-10-06 GitLab announced the \"governed software factory\". — https://about.gitlab.com/press/releases/2026-10-06-gitlab-announces-the-foundation-for-the-governed-software-factory/\n  - \nAnthropic's Claude Mythos 5 and 5.1 will power new Duo Agent Platform security flows\n.\n  - \nArtifact Central is in beta on GitLab.com, with Self-Managed availability planned for later in October\n. — https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/gitlab-announces-foundation-governed-software-130400498.html\n  - GitLab claims \nup to 50% lower total cost of ownership versus alternative tooling\n. This is a company claim.\n- The Transcend blog lists \n/goal flows, GitLab for Slack and the MCP Server as GA in October\n. — 2026-10-06 — https://about.gitlab.com/blog/transcend-india-announcements/\n- It also lists \nGitLab-hosted open-weight models (GLM 5.3, Kimi K3, MiniMax 3) as GA\n. — 2026-10-06 — same URL.\n- Pricing: \nGitLab.com rate limits will align to subscription tier starting October 19, 2026, with Premium and Ultimate moving in January 2027\n. — 2026-10-19 — https://about.gitlab.com/blog/rate-limit-change-2026/\n- Competition: I found no new competitor or share-shift news in the window. Earlier concerns were from Cantor on 2026-01-07, \nciting competition from GitHub and Atlassian\n (https://www.investing.com/news/analyst-ratings/gitlab-stock-rating-downgraded-by-cantor-fitzgerald-amid-competition-concerns-93CH-4435414).",
